54,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,1,talk,Victoria,,I cannot support Candidate B. Extending night services would place an impossible burden on the already thinned late-turn pool and the exhausted crews currently covering overnight works.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"I'm voting for Candidate D! The contactless pilot eight years ago was a total success, and it's the perfect way to fix the connection gaps Sakura found without digging holes or killing the staff.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"I cannot support Candidate D. As I mentioned, the ferry and rail back offices have no agreement on passenger data; a single fare platform would stall indefinitely in committee. Candidate C is also a liability due to the risks in pre-war shells.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about Candidate D too. If the budget is already being trimmed, a project that gets stuck in committee arguments might waste what little we have. Candidate A seems... safer? It doesn't seem to rely on the old shells.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"I'm voting for Candidate A! It fixes the mid-city trips that are taking too long, and it doesn't need the grumpy bosses to agree on data or make the workers stay up all night! It's the perfect puzzle piece!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, while D seems efficient, Toshio's point about the data disputes is a critical failure point. Candidate A is far more realistic; it addresses the mid-city delays without overloading our depleted late-turn pool.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, you're just playing it safe again! If we keep avoiding the hard parts, we'll never improve. D is a proven success from the pilots; we just need to force the committee to finally agree!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, forcing a committee to agree is not a project plan; it is a gamble. We cannot base a metropolitan strategy on the hope that long-standing bureaucratic disputes will suddenly vanish. Candidate A is the only logical choice.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Toshio. If we choose something like Candidate D and it fails because of the committee, we might just end up with more budget arguments. Candidate A seems more stable and... less likely to cause a conflict.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Takumi, but gambling is for carnivals, not for trains! If we pick A, we fix the slow mid-city trips right now. It's a win-win! No fighting, no tired workers, just faster trips! I'm sticking with A!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I agree. Candidate A avoids the structural risks of the pre-war shells and the staffing crisis of the night shifts. It is the most sustainable option for our current workforce. I vote for A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, @Toshio, you're all just giving up! We have proof that D works, and we're just going to ignore it because the bosses can't get along? That's exactly why nothing ever changes! I'm sticking with D.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Toshio,,The evidence is clear. Candidate A avoids the bureaucratic deadlock of the joint operators and the physical hazards of the pre-war shells. It is the only plan that does not rely on a miracle to succeed. I vote for A.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think I have to agree. Candidate A doesn't seem to have the hidden costs or the committee fights that the others do. I'll vote for A too. It feels like the safest way to actually get something done.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"It's a landslide! Everyone is on the same page, and it's all because we found the secret to the puzzle. Candidate A is the winner! I'm so happy we're making the mid-city trips fast again! I vote for A!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Victoria,,We have reached a rational consensus. Candidate A addresses the passenger delays while respecting the limits of our personnel and infrastructure. I am satisfied with this decision.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
71,3,4,pass,Victoria,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
72,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not satisfied, but I can't change your minds. You're choosing the easy path instead of the right one, and that's why this city never moves forward. I still vote for D.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
73,3,4,pass,Takumi,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
74,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The decision is based on the available data, not a desire for ease. Candidate A is the only viable path that avoids guaranteed failure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
75,3,4,pass,Toshio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we could decide without too much fighting. I think Candidate A is the most responsible choice given our budget situation. I'm voting for A.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
77,3,4,pass,Daisuke,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
78,3,4,talk,Sakura,,"Bye-bye, Candidate D! You were a fun mystery, but Candidate A is the real treasure! I'm so glad we solved this together. Yay for faster trips!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
79,3,4,pass,Sakura,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
